# ─── Upstream clones ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are unmodified public repositories, pinned by commit SHA in
# UPSTREAM.md. They are deliberately NOT vendored here — re-create them with
# scripts/fetch_upstream.sh. Local fixes live in patches/ instead.
AnalogGenie/repo/
AnalogGenie/repo
AnalogGym/repo/
AnalogGym/repo
AutoCkt/repo/
CktGNN/repo/
Krylov-ICML2023/repo/
LaMAGIC2/repo/
extensions/AnalogSAGE/
extensions/CircuitSense/
extensions/RoSE/
extensions/ZeroSim/
misc/AnalogGenie-Lite/
misc/AnalogToBi/
misc/ZOAF/

# ─── Large binaries ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Over or near GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, or re-downloadable.
# See "Files not tracked" in README.md for where each one comes from.
_wsl/*.wsl
LaMAGIC2/ckpt/
LaMAGIC2/data/

# ─── Claude Code worktrees ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session worktrees live here; they are checkouts of this same repo and must
# never be committed into it.
.claude/worktrees/

# ─── ngspice run artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rewritten on every run that touches a BSIM4 model, wherever ngspice is invoked.
bsim4v5.out

# ─── LNA experiment artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerable: sampled sequences and emitted netlists. The meta.json files are
# kept because they carry the timing and termination stats behind FINDINGS.md.
lna/out/*/seq*.txt
lna/out/*.pth
lna/out/templates_train.json
lna/out/winners_train.json
lna/work/
# Scratch driver logs + intermediate JSON from ad-hoc campaign runs (the `_`
# prefix is the convention for "throwaway, reproducible from a committed
# script"), the `.pre_*` backups the emitters write before overwriting a
# training set, and the per-iteration training-set snapshots. The durable record
# is the append-only label store (lna/data/*.jsonl) plus lna/data/reports/.
lna/out/_*
lna/out/*.pre_*.json
lna/out/*_train_*.json

# engineer line: per-cell throwaway trajectory files score_run.py writes before
# appending them into the canonical (committed) engineer/data/trajectories.jsonl
# in one serial pass. Same `_` throwaway convention: reproducible from the
# committed runner + result JSONs; the durable record is the canonical table.
engineer/data/_*

# ─── Runtime deps junctioned into a worktree ──────────────────────────────
# `misc/ZOAF`, `AnalogGenie` (Dataset .npy) and `AutoCkt/repo` (the 45 nm model
# include) are untracked upstream clones that exist only in the main checkout,
# so a fresh `git worktree` has none of them and every ngspice op silently
# returns None ("0 conducting" everywhere). Junction them in — verified NOT to
# appear in `git status`, so no ignore rule is needed for them:
#   New-Item -ItemType Junction misc         -Target <repo>\misc
#   New-Item -ItemType Junction AnalogGenie  -Target <repo>\AnalogGenie
#   New-Item -ItemType Junction AutoCkt\repo -Target <repo>\AutoCkt\repo

# Label store (plans2/01-DATA §2): L2/L1 tables + snapshots are precious and
# stay in git; the point-row table is a bulky, regenerable-ish byproduct.
lna/data/sim_points.jsonl
# The op-row table (plans2/09-WP-OBSERVE): same reason, more so -- an op row is
# ~5x a point row, because it carries every device's operating point and every
# node voltage instead of one metric vector.
lna/data/op_points.jsonl

# ─── Python / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
lna/out/winners_train.*.json

# self-contained conda prefix (local port to RHEL box)
.env/
env.sh

# engineer-line bulk trajectory tables: filesystem-only (E-5 ruling: raw data via DOI deposit, not the repo)
engineer/data/trajectories.jsonl
engineer/data/ext_trajectories.jsonl
engineer/data/ext_ldo_trajectories.jsonl
engineer/data/e6_trajectories.jsonl
engineer/data/e6_ext_trajectories.jsonl

# engineer-line bulk per-cell result JSONs (E-5 ruling: raw data via DOI deposit,
# not the repo; the filesystem copy is the resume state). Boards e6_*_v0.json and
# the runner .py stay tracked; only the per-cell arm×seed cells are ignored.
engineer/data/e6_incumbent_*.json
engineer/data/e6_racing_*.json
engineer/data/e6ext_amp_*.json
engineer/data/e6ext_ldo_*.json
